4 small holding tabs on each part.\n\nAssembly\n- Break the parts off their tabs and sand the tab marks.\n- Push the bars into the slots of one side plate, then fit the other plate on the free ends.\n\nBefore cutting for real\n- The slots are made for 9 mm material: measure your plywood (it is often a little thinner), set the Thickness field in the Stock panel and change the slot widths to match, or the bars will be loose.\n- Set X0 Y0 at the lower-left corner and Z0 on the top of the stock, and tick \"Air cut\" for a first run.","act":1,"oid":1}}